# ⚡ Volt

**A Jarvis-style AI assistant that runs on your own Windows PC.** Talk to it, show it things through your webcam, let it recognize your face, and message it from your phone. Free to run, written in Python.

> Volt is a hobby project built by a young developer. It works well, but it is not a finished commercial product. Please read [Safety and privacy](#safety-and-privacy) before you turn on the camera, screen, email or phone features.

---

## What Volt can do

| | |
|---|---|
| 🗣 **Talk to it** | Say "Hey Volt" and ask for anything. It listens, thinks, and answers out loud. |
| 👁 **See through your webcam** | Ask "what do you see?" and Volt describes what the camera shows. |
| 🙂 **Recognize faces** | Teach it who you are. It can greet you by name and even unlock itself with your face. |
| 🖥 **Look at your screen** | Ask for help with an error on screen, or let it quietly watch for problems. |
| 📱 **Message it from your phone** | Chat with Volt through a private Discord bot while it runs on your PC. |
| 📧 **Its own email** | Give Volt a mailbox of its own so it can check and send email without touching your personal inbox. |
| 🌤 **Live info** | Real weather and forecast, live sports scores, web search, and a daily briefing. |
| 🛠 **Get things done** | Reminders, timers, a to-do list, notes, clipboard, files, and shell commands. |
| 🧠 **Remembers you** | It keeps notes between sessions, and you can change its personality with `/mode`. |

Everything is optional. Camera, screen, email and phone access are all **off until you turn them on**.

## Quick start

You need a Windows 10/11 PC, Python 3.10 or newer, and a free [Groq](https://console.groq.com) API key. Full steps are in **[SETUP.md](SETUP.md)**. The short version:

```powershell
python -m pip install -U groq pyttsx3 psutil pyperclip edge-tts ddgs sounddevice numpy
setx GROQ_API_KEY your_key_here        # then close and reopen PowerShell
python agent_windows.py
```

The first time you run it, Volt asks you to create your profile.

## Commands

Type these inside Volt:

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `/hey` | Turn on the microphone for "Hey Volt" |
| `/voiceprint` | Teach Volt your voice so it ignores other people |
| `/camera on` | Allow the webcam (then just ask "what do you see?") |
| `/live` | Live camera window that greets you and checks in while you work |
| `/face enroll <name>` | Teach Volt a face (only people who agree!) |
| `/face unlock on` | Log in with your face |
| `/screen on` | Allow screen vision |
| `/phone` | Set up the Discord phone bot |
| `/email setup` | Give Volt its own mailbox (Gmail, GMX, Yahoo or custom) |
| `/fast` · `/smart` | Switch between the fast and the smarter AI model |
| `/mode` | Change Volt's personality |
| `/clear` | Start a fresh conversation |
| `exit` | Quit |

## Safety and privacy

Please read this part. Volt is powerful, and that comes with responsibility.

- **Volt can run commands and edit files on your PC when you ask it to.** It does not stop to ask "are you sure?" first. Only run it on a computer you're comfortable with, and don't ask for anything you wouldn't type yourself.
- **Your API key stays on your PC.** It lives in your Windows environment variables. Never post it, share a screenshot of it, or put it in a video.
- **The camera and screen are opt-in and off by default.** When you ask Volt what it sees, the picture is sent to the Groq AI service to be described. Nothing is saved as a file.
- **Face recognition stores numbers, not photos.** Only a numeric fingerprint of each face is kept, in a file on your PC. Only enroll people who agree, and delete anyone with `/face forget <name>`.
- **Email is read-only and untrusted.** Volt reads the inbox without marking mail as read, and it treats anything inside an email as untrusted text. Use a **separate mailbox for Volt**, not your personal one. Never use your main email password.
- **Phone access has a safe mode (on by default).** Messages from your phone can't run shell commands, read or write files, send email, or use the camera or screen. You can turn safe mode off, but think carefully before you do.
- **Don't share your Discord bot token.** If it leaks, reset it in the Discord Developer Portal.

## Free-tier limits

Groq's free tier limits how much you can use per minute and per day. Volt switches to its other model automatically when one is rate-limited, and keeps requests small, but heavy use (especially with the live camera and screen features) can still hit the limit. A paid Groq plan raises it.

